#index.html must never be cached long-term: it references the hashed
#/assets/* bundles. A stale cached index.html can point at a bundle the new
#build deleted, and Cloudflare's SPA fallback then hands the browser an HTML
#document as if it were JavaScript — a black page until a reload.
#Hashed assets, on the other hand, are immutable and can be cached forever.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
